From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:30:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/18] fitz: Stop the long steps of an aborted page run early.

A cookie abort was only noticed by the PDF interpreter between two
operators, so one long operator (decoding or scaling a large image,
rasterizing a huge path, converting an image through a tint transform,
building an ICC transform) ran to its end after the abort. For a
10200x14031 JPEG 2000 image drawn at full size that took seconds.

While a page is run with a cookie, the context points to cookie->abort
(fz_set_abort_flag, set and restored by fz_run_page_contents, annots,
widgets and document structure); the flag is also recorded for the
calling thread (fz_thread_abort_requested) for code that gets no
context.

Steps whose result may be stored throw FZ_ERROR_ABORT (fz_check_abort):
images are read from their decode chain in bands, the subarea,
subsample and unpack readers check on every call, JPEG 2000, JBIG2
(also the shared globals) and progressive JPEG stop inside the decoder
through the abort hooks of the OpenJPEG and jbig2dec patches and the
libjpeg progress monitor, decode arrays, colour keys and shading
functions are evaluated with checks, and an ICC transform built during
an abort is not stored (the lcms2 patch stops its slow building steps).

Steps that only draw stop early (fz_abort_requested): image scaling and
painting, pixmap painting and blending, glyph drawing, path flattening
and scan conversion, shading triangles and pixmap colour conversion
(ICC, separations, Lab). Pattern tiles and glyphs drawn during an abort
are not cached, and a run without a cookie (patterns, type3 glyphs)
throws instead of ending normally.

An abort never ends in an incomplete or more expensive result that
could be stored: fz_available, fz_read_byte, fz_peek_byte, fz_read_best,
the font and type3 glyph loaders let FZ_ERROR_ABORT through, and the
reduced resolution JPEG 2000 decode is not retried at full resolution.
When the colour key step of a JPEG 2000 image fails, the decoded image
is dropped too (it was leaked). Without an abort the output is
unchanged.

This patch uses the abort hooks added by the OpenJPEG, jbig2dec and
lcms2 patches (0006, 0007, 0008).

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
